{"path":"numeric/complex/sin","title":"std::sin(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>sin<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::complex)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/sin","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex sine of a complex value z.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> sin<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex sine of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, the complex sine of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned.\n</p><p>Errors and special cases are handled as if the operation is implemented by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span><code>&nbsp;</code><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/sinh\"><code>std::sinh</code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> z<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, where <code>i</code> is the imaginary unit.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The sine is an entire function on the complex plane, and has no branch cuts.\n</p>\nMathematical definition of the sine is <span class=\"texhtml\">sin z = <span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>e<span class=\"t-su\">iz<br></span>-e<span class=\"t-su\">-iz<br></span></td></tr><tr><td>2i</td></tr></table></span></span>.\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// behaves like real sine along the real line</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"sin\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\"><span class=\"kw1341\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" ( sin(1) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\"><span class=\"kw1341\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// behaves like sinh along the imaginary line</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"sin\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\"><span class=\"kw1341\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (sinh(1) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sinh\"><span class=\"kw1348\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sinh</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>sin(1.000000,0.000000) = (0.841471,0.000000) ( sin(1) = 0.841471)\nsin(0.000000,1.000000) = (0.000000,1.175201) (sinh(1) = 1.175201)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/cos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>cos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes cosine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\cos{z}}\">cos(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/tan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\tan{z}}\">tan(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc sine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arcsin{z}}\">arcsin(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sin</span><span>sinf</span><span>sinl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes sine (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\sin{x}}\">sin(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/sin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\">std::sin</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/csin\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>csin</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::sin(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Computes complex sine of a complex value z."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, the complex sine of z is returned."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The sine is an entire function on the complex plane, and has no branch cuts."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"cos(std::complex)","note":"computes cosine of a complex number (cos(z))"},{"label":"tan(std::complex)","note":"computes tangent of a complex number (tan(z))"},{"label":"asin(std::complex)","note":"computes arc sine of a complex number (arcsin(z))"},{"label":"sin, sinf, sinl","note":"computes sine (sin(x))"},{"label":"sin(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::sin to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":236,"codeBlockCount":2}
